  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Together for the Protection and Economic Empowerment of Youth in Thailand/TUI Academy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project provides youth with sustainable, decent economic opportunities in TUI&#x2019;s direct sphere of influence: TUI Hotels &amp; Resorts. The target group for the TUI Academy is 150 youth (aged 18-24, at least 60% young women) with low levels of education, at risk of exploitation or already working in exploitative situations. These youngsters take part in life skills training, market oriented vocational training, an internship and will be coached towards a decent job in the Tourism &amp; Hospitality (T&amp;H) sector, as well as follow a basic entrepreneurship training to increase their economic empowerment when T&amp;H work related opportunities are less prevalent (e.g. low seasons, natural disasters, etc.). 150 children in school (aged 5-17) receive age-appropriate life skills training to strengthen their self-esteem and reduce their vulnerability to exploitative situations. It is envisaged that by the end of the project at least 135 youth at risk will have the skills to succeed and at least 100 youth will be employed in a decent work opportunity, able to be self-reliant and support their families. The project is in Phang Nga province which is next to Phuket province. Both provinces are a high-risk area for severe forms of child labour and a priority destination of TUI. In September 2022, Thailand&#x2019;s Ministry of Tourism and Sports has joined hands and signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with 20 government agencies and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) to promote Child Safe Tourism Friendly Project. This includes developing measures to prevent human trafficking and all forms of sexual exploitation of children. It has been found that sexual exploitation of children is not a priority of the authorities and other stakeholders in Phang-Nga, while labour trafficking (especially from Myanmar) has received higher attention. Ethnic minorities are vulnerable to various forms of violence, including sexual exploitation. Since tourism in Phang-Nga is largely concentrated in Khao Lak area, the project focuses its activities to increase due diligence processes of tourism companies, multi-stakeholder cooperation and youth advocacy in Takuapa district where workers live and tourism is concentrated.</narrative>
  </description>
